I don't think so. Even in the quasi-real world of
Wicca, an athame is a wizard's weapon with which a
mystical bond exists, and so it is also in all of
literature. Denying the wizard expert status with
daggers is a denial of a big part of wizardry.

Besides, the NetHack wizard just is NOT the AD&D
wizard, with three other _intelligent_ party members
fully aware that the survival of the whole party
depends on keeping between the wizard and any chance
of melee. NetHack pets go wandering off in the
weeds, get too busy noshing to notice the wizard in
combat and in need of help, fall down trapdoors and
die with depressing regularity. The NetHack wizard
is thus frequently reduced to surviving only on
his/her own resources, unlike the AD&D wizard. Spell
points run out, if that is the only mechanism of
combat one has. In my (blundering and incompetent)
experience, a wizard without a small stack of
daggers at "expert" is not going to survive long
enough to find enough useful spellbooks to make
spellcasting a survival tool.  Nymph mirrors alone
make an expert missile weapon a necessity of life. A
wizard who forcebolts nymphs is soon a dead wizard.

IMO

